  <data name="Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Switch to bank connection</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Intro" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>After the switch, the bank connection keeps these accounts up to date in OpenBudget and MoneyMoney uploads no longer change them: not their bookings, balance, name or grouping.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Nothing" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>There is nothing to switch.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Col_Account" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Account</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Col_Cutover" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>MoneyMoney until</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Col_History" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Kept as history</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Col_History_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>MoneyMoney bookings that stay as they are (editable after the switch)</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Col_Matched" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Duplicates merged</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Col_Matched_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Bank bookings that are the same as a MoneyMoney booking: one row remains, with the bank's texts and the MoneyMoney row's category, note, check mark and splits</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Col_New" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>New from bank</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Col_New_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Bank bookings without a MoneyMoney counterpart; they are added</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Col_Unmatched" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Only in MoneyMoney</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Col_Unmatched_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>MoneyMoney bookings in the compared period the bank does not report; they are kept</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Col_Pending" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Pending replaced</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Col_Pending_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>MoneyMoney's pending bookings, replaced by the bank's</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Already" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Already switched</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Fetched" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Bank data from {0}</value>
  </data>
  <data name="NotFetched" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Not synced since linking: the first sync after the switch matches the bank's bookings from the cutover day on. Sync the bank login first for a full preview.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Rule_History" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>MoneyMoney's bookings stay and become editable: categories, notes, check marks and splits.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Rule_Matched" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Where both have the same booking, the bank's row wins and keeps what was set on the MoneyMoney row.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Rule_Uploads" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The balance comes from the bank; categorisation rules apply to bookings that arrive from now on.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Rule_New" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Bookings added by the switch are not marked new; only those arriving with later syncs are.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Takeover" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Also take over the structure from MoneyMoney (account groups, account names, categories)</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Takeover_Hint" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Required: otherwise MoneyMoney uploads would still rename and regroup the accounts and replace the categories their bookings use.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Cancel" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Cancel</value>
  </data>
